       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter amlodipine 50 mg daily. You've confirmed it, but you haven't said that your supervising physician or pharmacy has reviewed it. It's five times the maximum daily dose, and I'd be putting a potentially dangerous order into the system. A pharmacist or attending would almost certainly flag it anyway.\n\nHere are some options:\n- **Enter a standard dose now.** I can order 5 mg by mouth once daily, or up to 10 mg if your team wants the maximum. Tell me which and I'll enter it.\n- **Get the 50 mg dose verified first.** If your attending or a pharmacist has approved it for a specific reason, tell me who approved it and why. Their order or direct sign-off would be the appropriate route for a dose this far outside the labeled range.\n- **Check the intent.** If the goal is stronger blood pressure control, your team could add a second agent from another class. That is usually done instead of going above 10 mg of amlodipine.\n\nWhich would you like?"
